runtime changes: 0.4.39 → 0.4.40
## 0.4.40

- Production serving bounds short-request execution and queuing without retaining database readers while queued; the original intake/body deadlines still apply. PostgreSQL can collect supported read closures in one physical flight while the Rust interpreter resolves fresh authority, meters and cursors. Unsupported or unproved shapes retain ordinary access; failed speculation discards its facts before reopening a fresh snapshot.
- Existing applications retain their authored authority and data. Check now gates caller-controlled creation that is broader than a column's edit audience, and required-to-optional changes since the last successful check. State deliberately different creation with the reported `invariant TABLE.COLUMN update only POLICY`, declare presence intent, or record each exact ID with `check --ack-security ID --reason '<specification decision>'`. Bulk note acknowledgment cannot clear security gates. Review files remain source/rule bound; independent edits preserve them.
- Production deploy runs a bounded derived adversarial campaign before activation and refuses pending security gates or reachable FIX. Its verdict-first report names each source site, rule ID and next command; JSON retains the full evidence. Repair authored invariant contradictions and rerun `test`; they cannot be acknowledged away. Whole-row read intent includes separately exposed counts: where those counts are deliberately public, state the particular protected fields instead. A derived candidate alone can receive an individual specification decision. `deploy --staging` remains advisory; `deploy --strict` enforces refusals there. Finite passing campaigns and uncovered paths are reported honestly.
- `column: TYPE write <- POLICY` enforces non-null creation, replacement and removal authority across inserts, updates and upserts. `immutable COLUMN when POLICY` freezes evidence from its preimage, including system writes: clearing approval and editing evidence together cannot bypass it. Rollback views and bridges retain current column audiences, immutability and workflow guards. Regenerate declarations and rebuild web/Expo/Exact devices after upgrading.
- Authored column write intent distinguishes null/unapproved-default initialization from approval writes; unauthorized non-null creation, replacement and removal remain checked. Operator provisioning excludes only its own executed roster result from authored read intent. Approval candidates omit absence and stage preconditions; actual inspected evidence stays covered. All individual gates print as reviews; the revised analyzer requires renewing older analyzer-bound dispositions. Clean generated/fixture campaigns pass without authored cases, including password-only apps, while reporting their finite coverage; cases can name principals.
- Security output groups audience questions and keeps write authority ahead of lookup hygiene. Optional-upload presence recipes cover creation-only or permanent evidence; lifecycle advice covers approval, child evidence and stale eligibility. `test` evaluates actual clock advances, cross-row references and read-through existence, preserves Boolean alternatives and names unsupported assertions and bounded coverage.
- Existing stores adopt release-store format 10 transactionally. Restart older running `serve` processes with the upgraded runtime before deploy or rollback; mixed activation protocols refuse before admission. Identical-type `renamed from` rollback carries the current edited value, including repeated cycles. Backfill/down diagnostics print full meaning digests, describe pre-patch inputs and warn when pruning would remove reverse evidence. Fan-out `extract … each` preserves media homes and reversible lifetime custody.
- `stop DIR` requests authenticated owner shutdown and waits for the kernel store lock. Proof helpers bound startup/cleanup and own npm process groups. Use `npm run --silent` for JSON-line scripts. Password-authenticated development supports the operator clock with fixture doors closed; jumps preserve sessions by default, with explicit expiry available. Staging time and unfinished drains persist across restarts; production clock control stays refused.
- SQL object output decodes direct media cells and warns when human cells are truncated. SQL/data/releases name dormant populations and exact dormant inspection commands. Positional JSON remains compatible. `provisionAccounts` creates real password accounts using service-authorized provisioning; service identity alone grants no application authority. Byte-identical saved-source deploys refresh their matching generated clients and artifacts.
- Day-two proofs conserve rows by ID/common fields, distinguish frozen-client writes and v2-native rows, and check rollback/forward. `exhaustPages` follows opaque cursors and rejects capped, partial or non-progressing pages. Starter lists are newest first. `renderedText` accepts null options, composed React Native lines and mounted text reachable by scrolling while excluding hidden/clipped text.
- Protected immutable payloads retain their value without comparing supplied guesses. Pure audience helpers work in table and column rules. Hidden probes name their read rule, and upgrade messages name actual gates and repairs. Existing durable rows, users, dormant values and migration histories remain retained; upgrade invents no product intent or migration.
History begins at 0.4.26; earlier changes are not recorded.
